{"reference":"Proverbs 11","book":"Proverbs","chapter":11,"status":"pending","sections":[{"kind":"interpretive_questions","title":"Wealth and Fair Dealing","blocks":[{"id":"block_1","text":"Verse 1 warns against treating material gain as separate from fair dealing. Proverbs connects outcomes with diligence and choice, but it also condemns unjust scales and other ways of exploiting others. This keeps its sayings about wealth from being read as a simple guarantee that prosperity proves virtue.","verse_refs":["Proverbs 11:1"],"provenance_refs":["reader_path_proverbs_011_2b23ed6cd0a118607d430c33"],"confidence":"high","interpretation_level":"disputed"}]}],"generated_metadata":null}